   "text": "Parts pairing: whether the software lock that s5(c) forbids includes pairing that needs the maker's authorization.",
   "readings": [
    "U1-a: pairing that needs the maker's authorization is itself the lock s5(c) forbids; any part installed, genuine, salvaged or non-genuine, must work fully without contacting the maker, and makers must remove pairing from covered devices and leave it out of new ones",
    "U1-b: s3(a)(iv) presupposes that pairing continues; a lock is lawful if the owner (or a repairer acting for the owner) can pair a genuine part using a tool the maker supplies on fair and reasonable terms; makers may refuse to pair parts reported stolen and need not pair non-genuine parts"
